(4808583, 693005, 20608, '<td valign="top">well done Michelle. excellent</td>', 'well done Michelle. excellent', '2008-07-07 04:33:35.000000', NULL, 0),
(4808584, 693037, 62671, '<td valign="top">Nicely done!  Awww thanks for the comments.<br/></td>', 'Nicely done!  Awww thanks for the comments.', '2008-07-07 04:34:35.000000', NULL, 0),
(4808592, 692752, 68035, '<td valign="top">Very nice shot with amazing clarity in terms oof the sharpness of the filamaent.  Two great high contrast shots in a week.  One mibor thing is that the bulb does not seem quite straight, but I till you you should consider sticking this in a stock photography site because I am sure it would sell<br/> <br/>Great job</td>', 'Very nice shot with amazing clarity in terms oof the sharpness of the filamaent.  Two great high contrast shots in a week.  One mibor thing is that the bulb does not seem quite straight, but I till you you should consider sticking this in a stock photography site because I am sure it would sell Great job', '2008-07-07 04:49:03.000000', NULL, 0),
(4808594, 693005, 68035, '<td valign="top">Woot!!!!!  Look at you ribbon girl.  Great shot and the way you have combined clarity inside the bulb with a wonderful reflection on the glass is awesome.  A great idea brilliantly delivered and thoroughly deserving of the ribbon</td>', 'Woot!!!!!  Look at you ribbon girl.  Great shot and the way you have combined clarity inside the bulb with a wonderful reflection on the glass is awesome.  A great idea brilliantly delivered and thoroughly deserving of the ribbon', '2008-07-07 04:54:15.000000', NULL, 0),
(4808622, 693250, 9668, '<td valign="top">Just awesome. I feel like this should have done better.</td>', 'Just awesome. I feel like this should have done better.', '2008-07-07 05:37:57.000000', NULL, 0),
(4808655, 692788, 28962, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by bvy:</b></div><hr/><i> Abstract indeed. It''s a bit unlevel, and also would like to have seen the dark orange (above the yellow line) blend more with the black, making it less obvious just what this is. </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Your screen must be better than my screen(s).. On both it''s as black above as below the line.. <br/>Nevertheless, thanks for your comment..</td>', 'Originally posted by bvy: Abstract indeed. It''s a bit unlevel, and also would like to have seen the dark orange (above the yellow line) blend more with the black, making it less obvious just what this is.   Your screen must be better than my screen(s).. On both it''s as black above as below the line.. Nevertheless, thanks for your comment..', '2008-07-07 06:56:47.000000', NULL, 0),
(4808662, 693306, 9821, '<td valign="top">Nice finish, Robert ... excellent image</td>', 'Nice finish, Robert ... excellent image', '2008-07-07 07:19:09.000000', NULL, 0),
(4808670, 693005, 66384, '<td valign="top">Hooray!!! Congratulations!!! This is fantastic. Such beautiful clarity and color, and I agree the reflections really set this image apart as a winner.<br/> <br/>P.S. I have read the other comments and I do not see any evidence of the photographer in this reflection.<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2008-07-07 06:40:32.</i></td>', 'Hooray!!! Congratulations!!! This is fantastic. Such beautiful clarity and color, and I agree the reflections really set this image apart as a winner. P.S. I have read the other comments and I do not see any evidence of the photographer in this reflection.', '2008-07-07 07:35:32.000000', '2008-07-07 07:40:32.000000', 0),
(4808678, 692954, 91776, '<td valign="top">Congratulations Irene, another one blue ribbon.</td>', 'Congratulations Irene, another one blue ribbon.', '2008-07-07 07:52:51.000000', NULL, 0),
(4808802, 692954, 34938, '<td valign="top">irenechallenge wins again...it''s going to be unusual to not see you win a ribbon in every challenge you enter...this will be the new exception to the rule! <br/> <br/>Hey, I celebrate you Irene. You should do a book.<br/> <br/>Two things:<br/> <br/>1. You got a 1...who is the person that gave this a 1????<br/>2. How come you use a humble D50 when you have a D2X? Just asking...<br/> <br/>Your biggest fan,<br/> <br/>Enzo</td>', 'irenechallenge wins again...it''s going to be unusual to not see you win a ribbon in every challenge you enter...this will be the new exception to the rule!  Hey, I celebrate you Irene. You should do a book. Two things: 1. You got a 1...who is the person that gave this a 1????2. How come you use a humble D50 when you have a D2X? Just asking... Your biggest fan, Enzo', '2008-07-07 09:54:23.000000', NULL, 0),
(4808811, 692954, 86447, '<td valign="top">This is a good week for Irene!  :)  I''m thrilled for you.  Your images this week are excellent, as usual.<br/>I think I like this broken bulb better than your ''last burn'' one.  Congrats on the blue, Irene!</td>', 'This is a good week for Irene!  :)  I''m thrilled for you.  Your images this week are excellent, as usual.I think I like this broken bulb better than your ''last burn'' one.  Congrats on the blue, Irene!', '2008-07-07 10:01:24.000000', NULL, 0),
(4808817, 693005, 86447, '<td valign="top">This one was my fave for the challenge.   Technically well done and pretty to boot!  :)   Congrats on the ribbon, Michelle.<br/>(And thanks for all of your recent comments on my images during challenges.  You''re really working hard at commenting well.  It shows. )</td>', 'This one was my fave for the challenge.   Technically well done and pretty to boot!  :)   Congrats on the ribbon, Michelle.(And thanks for all of your recent comments on my images during challenges.  You''re really working hard at commenting well.  It shows. )', '2008-07-07 10:05:23.000000', NULL, 0),
(4808826, 692954, 52549, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by hotpasta:</b></div><hr/><i> irenechallenge wins again...it''s going to be unusual to not see you win a ribbon in every challenge you enter...this will be the new exception to the rule! <br/> <br/>Hey, I celebrate you Irene. You should do a book.<br/> <br/>Two things:<br/> <br/>1. You got a 1...who is the person that gave this a 1????<br/>2. How come you use a humble D50 when you have a D2X? Just asking...<br/> <br/>Your biggest fan,<br/> <br/>Enzo </i></td></tr></table> <br/>Hi Enzo, to answer your two questions:<br/>1. Don''t worry about the "1" giving person. I put a curse on him and he''s now the frog sitting on Lydias <img alt="'' . substr(''//www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/21_F.gif'', strrpos(''//www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/21_F.gif'', ''/'') + 1) . ''" border="0" src="//www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/21_F.gif"/> <a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/profile.php?USER_ID=86447" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">LydiaToo</a> light-bulb. He''ll never bother us again ;-D<br/>2.  The D50 is my absolute favourite camera. It sounds daft, I know (and I love the D2X) but everytime I pick up a camera, it''s nearly always the D50. I''m hoping I''ll grow out of it ;-D</td>', 'Originally posted by hotpasta: irenechallenge wins again...it''s going to be unusual to not see you win a ribbon in every challenge you enter...this will be the new exception to the rule!  Hey, I celebrate you Irene. You should do a book. Two things: 1. You got a 1...who is the person that gave this a 1????2. How come you use a humble D50 when you have a D2X? Just asking... Your biggest fan, Enzo  Hi Enzo, to answer your two questions:1. Don''t worry about the "1" giving person. I put a curse on him and he''s now the frog sitting on Lydias  LydiaToo light-bulb. He''ll never bother us again ;-D2.  The D50 is my absolute favourite camera. It sounds daft, I know (and I love the D2X) but everytime I pick up a camera, it''s nearly always the D50. I''m hoping I''ll grow out of it ;-D', '2008-07-07 10:10:56.000000', NULL, 0),
(4808858, 693005, 67697, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by JuliBoc:</b></div><hr/><i> P.S. I have read the other comments and I do not see any evidence of the photographer in this reflection. </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Thanks!  I couldn''t easily find my reflection in the bulb either lol  Guess I''m not too observant :D</td>', 'Originally posted by JuliBoc: P.S. I have read the other comments and I do not see any evidence of the photographer in this reflection.   Thanks!  I couldn''t easily find my reflection in the bulb either lol  Guess I''m not too observant :D', '2008-07-07 10:25:24.000000', NULL, 0),
(4808874, 693005, 61961, '<td valign="top">Congrats on your ribbon, Michelle!  It''s always fun to champion a photograph and then find out later the photographer is one of your online friends.<br/> <br/>I spent a couple minutes playing "find the photographer" in the reflection, but I don''t see you, either.</td>', 'Congrats on your ribbon, Michelle!  It''s always fun to champion a photograph and then find out later the photographer is one of your online friends. I spent a couple minutes playing "find the photographer" in the reflection, but I don''t see you, either.', '2008-07-07 10:33:02.000000', NULL, 0),
(4808935, 692954, 68599, '<td valign="top">aren''t you tired of winning? :P</td>', 'aren''t you tired of winning? :P', '2008-07-07 10:57:53.000000', NULL, 0),
(4808999, 692954, 86447, '<td valign="top">"Don''t worry about the "1" giving person. I put a curse on him and he''s now the frog sitting on Lydias light-bulb. He''ll never bother us again"<br/> <br/>Darn!  And I had him in my clutches and let him go...  *sigh*<br/> <br/>LOL!<br/></td>', '"Don''t worry about the "1" giving person. I put a curse on him and he''s now the frog sitting on Lydias light-bulb. He''ll never bother us again" Darn!  And I had him in my clutches and let him go...  *sigh* LOL!', '2008-07-07 11:45:30.000000', NULL, 0),
(4809038, 692954, 52549, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by cujee:</b></div><hr/><i> aren''t you tired of winning? :P </i></td></tr></table> <br/>Oh no, Jon. Definitely not. I still find it an exquisite pleasure to be in the top 10 of any challenge, especially with all the talent to be found here. I''m a nervous wreck all week when I have a good score and press the update button a million times. Nothing''s changed in that respect.  I love this site and the people on it.</td>', 'Originally posted by cujee: aren''t you tired of winning? :P  Oh no, Jon. Definitely not. I still find it an exquisite pleasure to be in the top 10 of any challenge, especially with all the talent to be found here. I''m a nervous wreck all week when I have a good score and press the update button a million times. Nothing''s changed in that respect.  I love this site and the people on it.', '2008-07-07 12:06:25.000000', NULL, 0),
(4809047, 693005, 70375, '<td valign="top">WOW!!! Congratulations on the ribbon!!!!! This is just awesome.</td>', 'WOW!!! Congratulations on the ribbon!!!!! This is just awesome.', '2008-07-07 12:11:46.000000', NULL, 0),
(4809072, 693005, 63398, '<td valign="top">Awesome image, Michelle!</td>', 'Awesome image, Michelle!', '2008-07-07 12:22:08.000000', NULL, 0),
(4809077, 693124, 52336, '<td valign="top">In response to your interest in others'' thoughts on this in the "personal best" thread, the thing that first strikes me here is the amount of space at the top of the frame.  Next I''m struck by the cramped composition below.  For me, it doesn''t make for a well-balanced photograph.  Stylistically, it''s a very interesting picture, and I think you''ve done well highlighting the form of your subject and contrasting its attractive transparency with the blocky, firm solidity of the clamp.  That''s nicely presented.  Overall though, the composition is in my opinion what prevents this photograph from being a 6.5 or higher.  I also think your post-processing (which I believe is what''s responsible for the "banding" in the negative space area at top) is somewhat overdone, though it could be said that it enhances the yellow already in this to present what seems to be an illuminated yet dark bulb.  Anyway, overall nicely done, and congratulations on your personal best.</td>', 'In response to your interest in others'' thoughts on this in the "personal best" thread, the thing that first strikes me here is the amount of space at the top of the frame.  Next I''m struck by the cramped composition below.  For me, it doesn''t make for a well-balanced photograph.  Stylistically, it''s a very interesting picture, and I think you''ve done well highlighting the form of your subject and contrasting its attractive transparency with the blocky, firm solidity of the clamp.  That''s nicely presented.  Overall though, the composition is in my opinion what prevents this photograph from being a 6.5 or higher.  I also think your post-processing (which I believe is what''s responsible for the "banding" in the negative space area at top) is somewhat overdone, though it could be said that it enhances the yellow already in this to present what seems to be an illuminated yet dark bulb.  Anyway, overall nicely done, and congratulations on your personal best.', '2008-07-07 12:23:21.000000', NULL, 0),
(4809090, 692954, 73235, '<td valign="top">Irene, you''re making it difficult for us to find more praises and compliments :) Congratulations to a brilliant and simple picture.<br/>Great job with the frog and the 1-voter!!<br/>Now we know what to do with trolls :)</td>', 'Irene, you''re making it difficult for us to find more praises and compliments :) Congratulations to a brilliant and simple picture.Great job with the frog and the 1-voter!!Now we know what to do with trolls :)', '2008-07-07 12:29:10.000000', NULL, 0),
(4809189, 692954, 68573, '<td valign="top">Irene,Irene,Irene.. wow you seem to be everywhere. You got an amazing talent ! It''s wonderful to see your work landing up so frequently with a ribbon and you are having a ''scalvertish'' run for the ribbons. Keep up the tempo.</td>', 'Irene,Irene,Irene.. wow you seem to be everywhere. You got an amazing talent ! It''s wonderful to see your work landing up so frequently with a ribbon and you are having a ''scalvertish'' run for the ribbons. Keep up the tempo.', '2008-07-07 13:27:14.000000', NULL, 0),
(4809193, 693250, 52500, '<td valign="top">Looks like we had the same idea!  Congrats on your great score and placement.  I guess the voters liked your no-water-line version better. :)</td>', 'Looks like we had the same idea!  Congrats on your great score and placement.  I guess the voters liked your no-water-line version better. :)', '2008-07-07 13:29:17.000000', NULL, 0),
